## UI Slice 2b-4 — Type-first note creation

Edit-capable users can create a new note from the vault sidebar: click **+ New note**, pick or type a `type` (a datalist offers existing types), enter a `name`, and the note is created and opened.

### What's in
- **`createNote` API** + **`useCreateNote`** mutation (invalidates the `['vault-tree', …]` query so the new note appears in the sidebar).
- **`NewNoteForm`** — type datalist + name input, client-side slug validation (`^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$`) on **both** fields *before* any network call, and server errors (409 collision / 400 invalid) surfaced via the shared `FormError` (`role="alert"`).
- **`VaultLayout`** — a `canEdit`-gated "New note" toggle; on success it closes the form and navigates to the created note.

### Grounded in the real backend
`POST /vaults/:id/notes {type,name}` is `edit`-gated, returns the created note (with its `path` to navigate to), 409s on collision, 400s on invalid slug. `type` is set at creation (immutable afterward via PUT — consistent with 2b-3).

### Permission-aware
The create affordance appears only for `edit`/`owner` vaults (reuses `canEdit`); read-only collaborators never see it.

### Out of scope (later)
Note rename/delete (2b-5), editing an existing note's type, live-preview, wikilinks. Also carried (non-blocking): the open form has no explicit cancel, and inputs aren't whitespace-trimmed.

